    <item>
      <title>iQoo Z9 Review</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/iqoo-z9-review/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 21 Dec 2024 15:00:00 +0530</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/iqoo-z9-review/</guid>
      
      <description>&lt;!-- &lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;iqoo-angry.gif&#34;
    alt=&#34;Photo Description&#34;&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;
      &lt;h4&gt;Photo Title&lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
 --&gt; 
&lt;figure style=&#34;text-align: center;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;tanjiro-iqoo.png&#34; alt=&#34;DNS logs of my iQoo Z9&#34; style=&#34;height: 100%; width: 80%;&#34;&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;div style=&#34;text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;TLDR; Hardware is as good as horrible is the software.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;
I bought an iQoo Z9 (8GB variant), and oh my god it has been a trauma. I am really dissatisfied with the phone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;yes-i-did-my-research-before-buying&#34;&gt;Yes, I did my research before buying!&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I knew iQoo doesn&amp;rsquo;t provide custom ROM support so was skeptical about it. I did my research over the internet but couldn&amp;rsquo;t find any good, detailed reviews other than those cringe Youtubers who never do proper analysis of phones. I was convinced with hardware specs but I was highly doubtful over the software experience as I was supposed to be the first iQoo buyer in my circle. Did my search queries on Reddit as well. Trust me I searched over Youtube, scrolled multiple pages on Google and other forums like XDA and no one mentioned problems in any proper review post.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
